.TH RZ0 1 "2026-08-10" "runtime.zero 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rz0 \- safety-led terminal-native system inventory and management foundation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rz0
.RI [ global-options ]
.br
.B rz0
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rz0
is the pre-alpha runtime.zero command-line and terminal interface. It is
report-first, dry-run-first, quarantine-first, and exact-confirmation-first.
Most product surfaces are read-only. There is no supported production release.
.PP
Bare invocation opens the interactive TUI only when standard input and output
are terminals and automation is not detected. Pipes, redirects, explicit
subcommands, and
.B --no-tui
remain scriptable.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --tui
Require the interactive TUI; fail rather than silently falling back.
.TP
.B --no-tui
Use the scriptable text dashboard.
.TP
.B --json
Use scriptable dashboard JSON where applicable.
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Select scriptable color policy. JSON never contains ANSI escapes.
.TP
.BR --version , " -V"
Print version information.
.TP
.BR --help , " -h"
Print command help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor [--format json]
Print privacy-safe configuration-bound diagnostics.
.TP
.B apps [--format text|json]
List bounded path-free installed-software evidence and source identifiers.
.TP
.B cache --dry-run [--fixture PATH] [--format text|json]
Review bounded ownership-aware cache evidence from known runtime/manager roots
or one local fixture. This is read-only and never authorizes cleanup,
quarantine, restore, or deletion.
.TP
.B cache --dry-run --plan --path ABSOLUTE_CACHE_FILE [--format text|json]
Build one exact, path-redacted, digest- and size-bound quarantine plan for an
explicit runtime.zero cache file. The plan is dry-run evidence and does not
move the file.
.TP
.B cache --apply --path ABSOLUTE_CACHE_FILE [--challenge-issued-unix-seconds SECONDS] [--confirm PHRASE] [--format text|json]
Without
.B --confirm,
print a short-lived challenge without writing. With the exact phrase, execute
only that one confirmation-bound quarantine move. It never deletes, recurses,
elevates, or uses network access.
.TP
.B leftovers --dry-run [--fixture PATH] [--format text|json]
Review bounded runtime.zero-owned module/log and unreferenced-receipt evidence or one local fixture. This
is read-only and never authorizes cleanup, quarantine, restore, or deletion.
.TP
.B leftovers --dry-run --plan --path ABSOLUTE_MODULE_FILE [--format text|json]
Build one exact, path-redacted, digest- and size-bound quarantine plan for an
explicit runtime.zero module-store file. The plan is dry-run evidence and does
not move the file.
.TP
.B leftovers --apply --path ABSOLUTE_MODULE_FILE [--challenge-issued-unix-seconds SECONDS] [--confirm PHRASE] [--format text|json]
Without
.B --confirm,
print a short-lived challenge without writing. With the exact challenge phrase
from a prior invocation, execute only that one confirmation-bound quarantine
move through the durable foundation journal and receipt path. It never deletes,
recurses, elevates, or uses network access; platform, retention, rollback, and
recovery gates still apply.
.TP
.B integrity --dry-run --fixture PATH [--format text|json]
.br
.B integrity --dry-run --path ABSOLUTE_FILE --sha256 DIGEST [--format text|json]
Review exact digest evidence from one local fixture or one bounded regular file.
The exact-file path is omitted from output. A trusted baseline is not configured;
this remains report-only and never authorizes remediation.
.TP
.B uninstall plan ID [--executable PATH] [--format text|json]
Build a live shared finding report and non-authorizing uninstall action plan.
An exact manager executable can make a manager action representable; no
uninstall executes.
.TP
.B scan --dry-run [--include-raw-paths] [--format text|json]
Collect bounded inventory. Raw paths are local-private and unsuitable for
support export.
.TP
.B monitor [--format text|json]
Print one native read-only resource snapshot.
.TP
.B toolchain [--format text|json]
Print Rust, AI, and developer-tool provider posture from bounded local evidence.
This command never invokes AIUP or another provider and never performs a write.
.TP
.B report [--format text|json]
Build a deterministic summary that omits raw paths, host/user identity,
application/service names, credentials, process output, and free-form warnings.
External sharing remains unauthorized pending review.
.TP
.B modules
List built-in core surfaces and explicitly installed module manifests.
.TP
.B modules validate MANIFEST [--format text|json]
Validate one local manifest without loading or executing code.
.TP
.B modules trust verify --manifest MANIFEST --signature ENVELOPE --trusted-test-key KEY [--format text|json]
Review exact local package integrity and a detached public test-key signature.
This is test-key-only, read-only evidence and never authorizes installation or
module execution.
.TP
.B modules install --dry-run PACKAGE [--format text|json]
Build a non-authorizing module lifecycle installation plan.
.TP
.B modules lifecycle-plan OPERATION --dry-run --module-id ID --from-state STATE --to-state STATE [--from-version VERSION] [--to-version VERSION] [--format text|json]
Render one digest-bound schema-1 module lifecycle plan. This is a review-only
surface; it does not publish registry state, execute code, or authorize a
lifecycle action. Supported operations are install, activate, invoke,
deactivate, repair, migrate, upgrade, and uninstall.
.TP
.B store plan|status|init
Inspect the local store or explicitly create only runtime.zero-owned user-local
scaffolding. Use
.B store init --yes
for the write path; unsupported platforms fail closed.
.TP
.B updates --dry-run ...
Review fixture, captured, or explicitly probed manager availability; optionally
build a finding-bound plan or serial queue.
.TP
.B updates --dry-run --all-providers --allow-network-read ...
Run the provider-driven review for installed managers, language/package
environments, known self-updaters, and declared application update metadata.
Missing, delegated, observed-only, and unsupported sources remain warnings;
this is not a claim of universal provider coverage.
.TP
.B updates --apply ...
Pre-alpha manager execution lane. It requires a fresh probe, network intent,
one exact action or interactive serial queue, a plan-sealed executable identity,
a platform identity-to-spawn binding, a short-lived exact confirmation, durable
journal/effect receipt, and fresh verification. Elevated managers use
non-interactive /usr/bin/sudo and require prior sudo authentication. Known
self-updaters may replace their launcher during a successful update.
.TP
.B updates --recovery-status --transaction ID [--format text|json]
Read and classify exact durable manager-effect evidence. It never retries,
completes, rolls back, edits, or removes state.
.TP
.B updates --recovery-complete --transaction ID [--challenge-issued-unix-seconds SECONDS] [--confirm PHRASE] [--format text|json]
Obtain or submit a fresh receipt-bound approval that appends only the final
local journal commit for a verified manager effect. It never reruns the manager,
rolls back, or authorizes automatic mutation.
.TP
.B completions SHELL
Print static completion source for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell. No shell
files are modified.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful command or a read-only challenge/status result.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, invalid evidence, unsupported safety gate, or fail-closed
operation.
.PP
A normal broken output pipe exits successfully.
.SH SAFETY
Do not treat a plan, signature, executable lease, confirmation, receipt,
finding, diagnostic, or release ledger as broader authority. Do not share raw
inventory without review. Never edit the runtime.zero state store manually to
bypass a recovery decision. Uninstall, recursive cleanup, module lifecycle
execution, third-party execution, and permanent deletion are not implemented
product actions. The leftovers apply lane is limited to one explicitly supplied
runtime.zero module-store file and remains subject to the exact confirmation,
foundation recovery, retention, and platform gates.
.SH FILES
Runtime paths are platform-specific user-local paths shown by
.B rz0 store plan .
The state root contains the installed registry, immutable transaction heads,
confirmation consumption, and receipts. Treat it as private local evidence.
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md, SAFETY.md, SECURITY.md, docs/documentation-index.md,
docs/project-status-and-resumption.md, docs/recovery-guide.md
.SH BUGS
Report security concerns privately as described in SECURITY.md. Do not include
credentials, private paths, customer data, or unreviewed inventory in a public
issue.
